A common use of a custom function is to call out the sign of values, perhaps in the table of changes
from earlier:

::: {#7f5143cf .cell execution_count=10}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def sign_colors(vals):
    return [
        None if x is None else "#1B9E77" if x > 0 else "#D95F02" if x < 0 else "#FFFFFF"
        for x in vals
    ]

(
    GT(changes_df)
    .data_color(columns="change", fn=sign_colors)
    .fmt_number(columns="change", decimals=1, force_sign=True)
)
```

